  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running it with Python gave the same number.\n\n1. `service2.compute_fee` imports only two modules: `pricing.base_fee` and `discounts.apply_discount`.\n2. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n3. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")`: gold is a 20% discount, so 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` (which would add 25% for gold) and `decoy_shipping.py` are never imported, so they don't affect the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
